{"term":"boring","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e2fef47c08af3f1606","definition":"The act or process of boring holes; such practice as an area of expertise in manufacturing.","example":"A warm, soft, tender, sweet sensation. It's much like anesthesia– And mysteriously, my trembling gradually starts to lessen. Her faint breaths tickle my cheek. A very sweet scent. I abruptly feel a pressure against my chest. The great sword she carries is tearing the skin of my chest, boring into my flesh, threading through my bones, and steadily sinking its way into my body. Yet, numbed by the anesthesia of the kiss, I no longer feel any pain. Because you kill me like this, so gently– I unexpectedly become anguished. I'm on the verge of crying. To keep her from noticing, I look past her head, up at the dark gray sky that goes on dropping rain on us.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["boring bit","macroboring","microboring"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boring#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:30c5c572d1e8f3cbf6","definition":"A pit or hole which has been bored.","example":"It is common in urban areas that a great many borings exist from prior construction work.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["boring bit","macroboring","microboring"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boring#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:795f783d2ae5e89efd","definition":"One of the fragments thrown up when something is bored or drilled.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["chip","swarf"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"plural-normally","register":"countable, plural-normally, uncountable","wordFamily